# Batch files are Windows-only and MUST arrive with CRLF endings.
#
# A .bat or .cmd saved with bare LF can execute its own REM banner as commands
# rather than skipping it - it fails silently and can create stray files. That
# was measured in a sibling repo on 2026-09-06, and the lesson worth keeping is
# that only RUNNING one found it: two separate probes read the endings as fine
# and both were false negatives.
#
# `eol=crlf` forces CRLF on checkout regardless of core.autocrlf or the
# platform, so this holds for a clone on any machine instead of depending on a
# local git setting that a fresh clone may not share. Every .bat/.cmd blob here
# is already stored LF-normalised, which is what this attribute expects, so
# adding it renormalises nothing and produces no churn.
#
# 🚫 Deliberately NOT `* text=auto`. That would renormalise the entire repo in
# one commit and bury every real change in the noise. This is scoped to the one
# file type where the wrong ending is not cosmetic but a genuine failure.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
